# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your own Sanity project's values
# once you've run `npx sanity init` (see README.md, Phase 1).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production

# Needed for any server-side read/write against the (private) production
# dataset — including the Facebook auto-post webhook's write-back of
# socialPostedAt below, which needs an Editor-level token, not just Viewer.
# Create one at manage.sanity.io -> API -> Tokens.
# SANITY_API_TOKEN=

# The site's own public URL, used to build absolute article links (Open
# Graph tags, and the link the Facebook auto-post webhook posts). Defaults
# to https://atoll-wire.vercel.app in lib/siteUrl.ts if unset — only set
# this if/when a custom domain is attached.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---- Facebook auto-posting (see README.md "Facebook auto-posting") ----
# Shared secret pasted into BOTH this env var and the webhook's "Secret"
# field in manage.sanity.io -> API -> Webhooks. Verifies that POSTs to
# /api/webhooks/sanity-publish really came from Sanity.
# SANITY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# The numeric ID of the AtollWire Facebook Page (not a personal profile —
# the Graph API can only post to Pages). Found under the Page's About tab,
# or via https://developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer.
# FB_PAGE_ID=

# A long-lived Page access token with the pages_manage_posts permission.
# Generate via a Meta Business app in the Graph API Explorer, then exchange
# the short-lived user token for a long-lived Page token — see README.md
# for the exact steps.
# FB_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
